29cdbfaff4c230e2,https://openalex.org/W3205972749,https://openalex.org/W3119866685,Taming Sparsely Activated Transformer with Stochastic Experts,Switch Transformers: Scaling to Trillion Parameter Models with Simple and Efficient Sparsity,7,EXPERIMENTS,name,unknown,"The experimental results in Table 1 show that performance of the Switch Transformer is on par with the vanilla Transformer, e.g., its average BLEU score on the 12 datasets is 26.3, the same as the Transformer.","mber of heads from 8 to 4 with the dimension of each head doubled. We use two experts for the expert-based models. We remark that even though THOR increases the number of parameters, its inference speed (in terms of FLOPs) is the same as Transformer-base because only one expert is activated for each input. Interested readers refer to Appendix C for more details. The experimental results in Table 1 show that performance of the Switch Transformer is on par with the vanilla Transformer, e.g., its average BLEU score on the 12 datasets is 26.3, the same as the Transformer. The results confirm that SAMs do not outperform densely activated models with similar model sizes. In contrast, THOR achieves more than 1.0 BLEU score improvement over the Switch Transformer in all the 12 tasks. THOR also significantly outperforms the models trained using the two competing regularization",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2110.04260#page=7,heuristic_unvalidated,23159
33fcf67c24e661d3,https://openalex.org/W3205972749,https://openalex.org/W3119866685,Taming Sparsely Activated Transformer with Stochastic Experts,Switch Transformers: Scaling to Trillion Parameter Models with Simple and Efficient Sparsity,7,EXPERIMENTS,name,unknown,"In contrast, THOR achieves more than 1.0 BLEU score improvement over the Switch Transformer in all the 12 tasks.","ed readers refer to Appendix C for more details. The experimental results in Table 1 show that performance of the Switch Transformer is on par with the vanilla Transformer, e.g., its average BLEU score on the 12 datasets is 26.3, the same as the Transformer. The results confirm that SAMs do not outperform densely activated models with similar model sizes. In contrast, THOR achieves more than 1.0 BLEU score improvement over the Switch Transformer in all the 12 tasks. THOR also significantly outperforms the models trained using the two competing regularization methods, SMART and R3F. 5.3 RICH-RESOURCE TRANSLATION We use two widely adopted rich-resource translation benchmarks: English to German translation from WMT’16 and English to French translation from WMT’14. The former dataset consists of 4.5 million training sentence pairs, and the latter 36 million pairs. We fo",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2110.04260#page=7,heuristic_unvalidated,23475
1b5ce6d9c3aec597,https://openalex.org/W3205972749,https://openalex.org/W3119866685,Taming Sparsely Activated Transformer with Stochastic Experts,Switch Transformers: Scaling to Trillion Parameter Models with Simple and Efficient Sparsity,7,EXPERIMENTS,author_year,unknown_negated_or_contrast,"Similar to what is observed in low-resource translation, the Switch Transformer (Fedus et al., 2021) does not outperform the vanilla Transformer (Ott et al., 2018).","used. Specifically, THOR lifts the previous state-of-the-art (Liu et al., 2020b;c) by 0.3 BLEU score on the En-De translation task and 0.1 BLEU score on the En-Fr translation task. THOR also significantly outperforms the models trained using the other two regularization methods, SMART (Jiang et al., 2020) and R3F (Aghajanyan et al., 2020). Similar to what is observed in low-resource translation, the Switch Transformer (Fedus et al., 2021) does not outperform the vanilla Transformer (Ott et al., 2018). Table 2: BLEU and sacreBLEU scores on WMT’14 En-Fr and WMT’16 En-De. Results of Jiang et al. (2020), Aghajanyan et al. (2020), and Fedus et al. (2021) are from our implementation. BLEU En-De En-Fr Vaswani et al. (2017) 28.4 41.8 Ott et al. (2018) 29.3 43.2 Wang et al. (2019b) 29.6 — Wu et al. (2019a) 29.7 43.2 So et al. (2019) 29.8 41.3 Jiang et al. (2020) 29.",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2110.04260#page=7,heuristic_unvalidated,24857
