96d3334775bcd453,https://openalex.org/W4224211001,https://openalex.org/W4224299101,On the Representation Collapse of Sparse Mixture of Experts,StableMoE: Stable Routing Strategy for Mixture of Experts,9,Related Work,author_year,background_section,Dai et al. (2022) propose to freeze the routing function in order to relieve routing fluctuation.,"; Du et al., 2021). SMoE Routing Algorithms Many recent studies explore the token assignment algorithms for SMoE routing. BASE layers (Lewis et al., 2021) formulate the token routing problem as a linear assignment problem. Hash Layers (Roller et al., 2021) employ a parameter-free assignment algorithm that routes tokens by hashing. Zhou et al. (2022) let each expert select top-k tokens rather than distribute tokens to experts. Dai et al. (2022) propose to freeze the routing function in order to relieve routing fluctuation. These methods focus on the assignment algorithm in routing, but our routing algorithm focuses on improving the underlying routing scoring metric, which is still under-explored. 9 Representation Collapse Representation collapse, also termed neural collapse, is the degeneration of the representations during the training of neural networks. Several",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2204.09179#page=9,heuristic_unvalidated,32687
