3f14bd618a0bbe6c,https://openalex.org/W4226515448,https://openalex.org/W3040573126,DeepSpeed-MoE: Advancing Mixture-of-Experts Inference and Training to Power Next-Generation AI Scale,GShard: Scaling Giant Models with Conditional Computation and Automatic Sharding,4,Related Work,numeric,background_section,"GShard [4] utilizes MoE to train a transformer-based model [26] to 600B parameters for multi-language translation, and it shows that the training cost of this 600B MoE model is even cheaper than that of a 100B dense model.","rements. 2.2 Reducing Training Cost by MoE Architecture One promising way to reduce the training cost is using Mixture of Expert (MoE) [24]. In [3] authors scale LSTM based model to 127B by applying convolutional MoE layers between stacked LSTM layers [25] for language modelings and machine translation. The sparsity nature of MoE significantly improves the scaling of model size without increasing the computational cost. GShard [4] utilizes MoE to train a transformer-based model [26] to 600B parameters for multi-language translation, and it shows that the training cost of this 600B MoE model is even cheaper than that of a 100B dense model. Switch Transformer [5] continues this based on the T5 model and scales the model to 1.6 trillion. To achieve same accuracy performance, [5] shows a 2.5x faster training speed of MoE models as compared to large dense m",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2201.05596#page=4,heuristic_unvalidated,10969
