7e981ac56907d02f,https://openalex.org/W4297631950,https://openalex.org/W3040573126,A Review of Sparse Expert Models in Deep Learning,GShard: Scaling Giant Models with Conditional Computation and Automatic Sharding,13,INTRODUCTION,author_year,unknown,"7.1 INSTABILITY Sparse models have frequently been reported to be more unstable, meaning the loss diverges and increases (Lepikhin et al., 2020; Fedus et al., 2021; Zoph et al., 2022; Mustafa et al., 2022).","U and GPU (see Section 2.2 for more details). Other approaches for reducing the memory footprint of sparse models are discussed in Section 7.3. 7 SPARSE MODEL TRAINING IMPROVEMENTS Sparse models often have different dynamics than dense models and benefit from different training and fine-tuning methodologies. 7.1 INSTABILITY Sparse models have frequently been reported to be more unstable, meaning the loss diverges and increases (Lepikhin et al., 2020; Fedus et al., 2021; Zoph et al., 2022; Mustafa et al., 2022). Instabilities also appear more often at larger model scales. Lepikhin et al. (2020) encountered training instability using bfloat16 activations with a 1 trillion parameter model. Fedus et al. (2021) encountered instabilities in their highest-compute Switch-XXL model. Zoph et al. (2022) encountered instabilities in their largest models, especially in the multi-",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2209.01667#page=13,heuristic_unvalidated,46459
