4dd4b8a3fc72ee2b,https://openalex.org/W4304697563,https://openalex.org/W2581624817,EvoMoE: An Evolutional Mixture-of-Experts Training Framework via Dense-To-Sparse Gate,Outrageously Large Neural Networks: The Sparsely-Gated Mixture-of-Experts Layer,4,unresolved,numeric,unknown,"[7] proposes the Top-K gating as Equation 5, which keeps only the top k values before the softmax function.","ch individual expert on xs, e.g., e0(xs), e1(xs) and e2(xs). By combining the gate’s output, i.e., [0.35, 0.65, 0], the output of this MoE layer is ys = 0.35 ∗e0(xs) + 0.65 ∗e1(xs). Sparse Gate Network: The sparse gate network G is the key component to introduce model sparsity, which takes a batch of tokens {x1, ..., xs} as input and produces the probability of them with respective to all experts {e1, ..., eN}. Shazeer et al. [7] proposes the Top-K gating as Equation 5, which keeps only the top k values before the softmax function. In addition, Wg is a trainable variable (Wg ∈RD×N) and determine the targeted experts for each token. g(xs) = softmax(TopK(xs · Wg)) (5) We illustrate the workflow of a MoE layer in Figure 3, where k = 2 and Wg is a 3 × 3 (i.e., feature dimension × number of experts) matrix to represents the parameter of gate network. We firs",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2112.14397#page=4,heuristic_unvalidated,17202
