34247011d13baa58,https://openalex.org/W4304697563,https://openalex.org/W3040573126,EvoMoE: An Evolutional Mixture-of-Experts Training Framework via Dense-To-Sparse Gate,GShard: Scaling Giant Models with Conditional Computation and Automatic Sharding,4,unresolved,numeric,unknown,"Distributed Training of MoE Models: Expert parallel training is a specific method of parallelism for MoE models, which is first proposed by GShard [9].","y Top-K gating on Long ShortTerM memory (LSTM) kayers [23] and Lepikhin et al. [9] introduced MoE with Top-2 gate into Transformer. Lewis et al. [10] adopted the numerous solution for balanced tokento-expert routing and Roller et al. [11] utilized the hash-based routing strategy. Distributed Training of MoE Models: Expert parallel training is a specific method of parallelism for MoE models, which is first proposed by GShard [9]. Experts are placed on different workers and each worker takes a different batch of training samples. For non-MoE layers, expert parallelism behaves the same as data parallelism. In MoE layers, tokens in the sequence are sent to workers where their desired experts reside. Similar to model parallelism, the outputs of each MoE layer are exchanged again to be organized back into original sequences for the computation of the next",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2112.14397#page=4,heuristic_unvalidated,18564
