cd1a6a381ae4be0e,https://openalex.org/W4378473852,https://openalex.org/W4200634402,Mixture-of-Experts Meets Instruction Tuning:A Winning Combination for Large Language Models,GLaM: Efficient Scaling of Language Models with Mixture-of-Experts,10,Related Work,numeric,background_section,"This approach allows an input to either select all experts [11] or merely a sparse mixture of them, as observed in recent massive language models [12, 10].","rise in computational expense. This is achieved by selectively activating only the relevant portions of the model, based on input-dependent factors. MoE models leverage a learned gating mechanism that triggers only a select subset of k experts out of a total of E for a given input. This approach allows an input to either select all experts [11] or merely a sparse mixture of them, as observed in recent massive language models [12, 10]. While a number of studies have sought to enhance the gating mechanism itself [15, 24, 43, 55], MoE models have also been explored in the context of multitask learning [15, 22]. Typically, a shared pool of experts is used, although there has been investigation into per-task routers [30]. This essentially permits an input to choose the most relevant expert(s) for a given task, thereby optimizing the processing and results. Nev",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2305.14705#page=10,heuristic_unvalidated,32875
