144e7597ed7c0d17,https://openalex.org/W4391591172,https://openalex.org/W4200634402,CompeteSMoE -- Effective Training of Sparse Mixture of Experts via Competition,GLaM: Efficient Scaling of Language Models with Mixture-of-Experts,1,Introduction,name,unknown_negated_or_contrast,"Furthermore, due to the large scale nature of LLM experiments, empirical evaluations are often restricted to the vanilla Transformer, which does not take into account the advanced architectures such as GLaM (Du et al., 2022) or Brainformer (Zhou et al., 2023).","theless, state-ofthe-art strategies mostly rely on intuitive conceptualizations, which can only offer greedy solutions such as using a cosine router (Chi et al., 2022) or a two-phase training procedure (Dai et al., 2022). Furthermore, due to the large scale nature of LLM experiments, empirical evaluations are often restricted to the vanilla Transformer, which does not take into account the advanced architectures such as GLaM (Du et al., 2022) or Brainformer (Zhou et al., 2023). This work focuses on improving the training effectiveness of SMoE by addressing its core challenge of representation collapse. To this end, we first seek to develop a reliable strategy to route inputs to experts. Motivated by the Winner-take-all (WTA) principle (Grossberg & Grossberg, 1982) originated from biology (Riesenhuber & Poggio, 1999; Andersen et al., 1969; Eccle",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2402.02526#page=1,heuristic_unvalidated,4033
