4bf2260fb03b4474,https://openalex.org/W4404133759,https://openalex.org/W3119866685,MoNDE: Mixture of Near-Data Experts for Large-Scale Sparse Models,Switch Transformers: Scaling to Trillion Parameter Models with Simple and Efficient Sparsity,2,INTRODUCTION,numeric,unknown,Recent studies show that Transformer-based models that adopt MoE (dubbed MoE Transformers) achieve substantial improvements in model performance over conventional dense Transformers [2].,"TIVATION 2.1 Mixture of Experts The Mixture of Experts (MoE) is an ensemble technique that aims to enhance model performance. The key motivation behind using MoE is to increase the model capacity without a proportional increase in computation. Recent studies show that Transformer-based models that adopt MoE (dubbed MoE Transformers) achieve substantial improvements in model performance over conventional dense Transformers [2]. Figure 1 shows a high-level overview of MoE Transformers, where MoE is applied to the feed-forward network (FFN) within the Transformer block. The MoE FFN layer combines multiple copies of dense FFNs, called experts. Each expert comprises two linear layers and an activation layer in between, which is the same as the FFN layer in conventional Transformer blocks. The key component in MoE is the gating/routing network, which de",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2405.18832#page=2,heuristic_unvalidated,7375
