fa3afd8e9720fd10,https://openalex.org/W4406703768,https://openalex.org/W4224211001,FSMoE: A Flexible and Scalable Training System for Sparse Mixture-of-Experts Models,On the Representation Collapse of Sparse Mixture of Experts,5,Routing,numeric,use_signal,"We pre-implement four routing functions: GShard routing [22], Sigmoid [8, 23] routing, X-MoE routing [6], and SoftMoE routing [36].","and 3) easy schedule of different tasks. 3.1 Modularization and Non-Invasive Modification In our FSMoE framework, the MoE layer is divided into six distinct sub-modules, namely: Gate, Order, I-Order, Dispatch, Combine, Expert. Gate: The Gate sub-module determines how tokens are assigned to different experts for calculation. We pre-implement four routing functions: GShard routing [22], Sigmoid [8, 23] routing, X-MoE routing [6], and SoftMoE routing [36]. Order & I-Order: The Order sub-module transforms the input tensor layout before it is dispatched. Typically, the format changes from (B, L, M) to (E,T, M). We pre-implement two ASPLOS ’25, March 30-April 3, 2025, Rotterdam, Netherlands Xinglin Pan et al. types of ordering functions: 1) GShard [22] ordering, which uses a combination of einsum and matrix multiplication, and 2) Tutel [17] ordering,",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2501.10714#page=5,heuristic_unvalidated,26318
