98a4a3857ee2833c,https://openalex.org/W4410427444,https://openalex.org/W4402671950,DeepSeek: Paradigm Shifts and Technical Evolution in Large AI Models,DeepSeekMoE: Towards Ultimate Expert Specialization in Mixture-of-Experts Language Models,8,Training,numeric,unknown,The existing MoE model faces two primary issues [40]: 1) Knowledge hybridity.,"ken, which is defined as gi,t = g′ i,t PNr j=1 g′ j,t , (4) g′ i,t = ( si,t, si,t + bi ∈Topk({sj,t + bj|1 ≤j ≤Nr}, Kr), 0, otherwise, (5) where si,t is the token-to-expert affinity, Topk(·, Kr) selects the top K affinity scores for the t-th token across routed experts, bi is a bias for each expert, used to balance load and model performance [105]. Compared with conventional MoE. The existing MoE model faces two primary issues [40]: 1) Knowledge hybridity. Existing MoE models typically use a small number of experts (e.g., 8 and 16). This means each expert may need to handle different types of knowledge, making it hard for them to specialize in one area. As a result, the expert’s parameters become too broad and less effective; and 2) Knowledge redundancy. In many cases, tokens assigned to various experts may require similar or overlapping knowledge [10",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2507.09955#page=8,heuristic_unvalidated,42026
