5717412b9057094b,https://openalex.org/W4417006825,https://openalex.org/W4408145414,SkyMoE: A Vision-Language Foundation Model for Enhancing Geospatial Interpretation with Mixture of Experts,RS-MoE: A Vision–Language Model With Mixture of Experts for Remote Sensing Image Captioning and Visual Question Answering,1,Introduction,author_year,unknown,"However, prior RS-based MoE models (Lin et al. 2025) have mostly adopted general-purpose arXiv:2512.02517v1 [cs.CV] 2 Dec 2025 SkyMoE (Ours) A basketball court is located at the center of the image.","entangle and properly integrate localized and contextual features, which undermines both model reliability and taskspecific performance. To address this issue, there is increasing interest in modular architectures that support specialization, such as Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) frameworks. MoE architectures offer structural flexibility by distributing computation across expert subnetworks. However, prior RS-based MoE models (Lin et al. 2025) have mostly adopted general-purpose arXiv:2512.02517v1 [cs.CV] 2 Dec 2025 SkyMoE (Ours) A basketball court is located at the center of the image. USER: Please briefly describe this image. There is a tennis court located close to each other in the center of the scene. GeoChat VHM This is a top-down view of a basketball court. USER: Where is the largest basketball court on the westernmost side ? Ground Truth Image Captio",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2512.02517#page=1,heuristic_unvalidated,4865
451b10fe859f3d0e,https://openalex.org/W4417006825,https://openalex.org/W4408145414,SkyMoE: A Vision-Language Foundation Model for Enhancing Geospatial Interpretation with Mixture of Experts,RS-MoE: A Vision–Language Model With Mixture of Experts for Remote Sensing Image Captioning and Visual Question Answering,3,Related Work,author_year,background_section,"For example, RS-MoE (Lin et al. 2025) employs an MoE structure to effectively fuse information from heterogeneous data sources, while RSUniVLM (Liu and Lian 2024) utilizes experts to specialize in different downstream tasks.","require a dynamic emphasis on either local or global information. This highlights that while the problem of feature balancing is recognized, a mechanism for dynamic, input-aware allocation of model resources remains a critical unfilled gap in RS-VLMs. Mixture of Experts for Remote Sensing The promise of MoE as a dynamic, learned framework has recently led to its adoption in the remote sensing domain. For example, RS-MoE (Lin et al. 2025) employs an MoE structure to effectively fuse information from heterogeneous data sources, while RSUniVLM (Liu and Lian 2024) utilizes experts to specialize in different downstream tasks. These pioneering works demonstrate the versatility of the MoE paradigm. However, in these existing frameworks, the MoE mechanism is primarily leveraged for multi-modal fusion or task-level specialization, rather than being explicitly d",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2512.02517#page=3,heuristic_unvalidated,11615
