b9f8c3be6d5b1e82,https://openalex.org/W7106330638,https://openalex.org/W4402671637,MoDES: Accelerating Mixture-of-Experts Multimodal Large Language Models via Dynamic Expert Skipping,Not All Experts are Equal: Efficient Expert Pruning and Skipping for Mixture-of-Experts Large Language Models,1,Introduction,numeric,unknown,"Nevertheless, MoE models typically struggle with suboptimal expert utilization [28, 42] due to a fixed number of activated experts for all tokens, which can incur significant inference inefficiency [28, 42, 66].","emerged as an effective solution to reduce the cost of large-scale MLLMs. By sparsely activating partial parameters (i.e., selected expert networks) for each token, MoE MLLMs [26, 50] decouple the factor of model size from computational costs. This design offers substantial computational savings without compromising performance [27, 36]. Nevertheless, MoE models typically struggle with suboptimal expert utilization [28, 42] due to a fixed number of activated experts for all tokens, which can incur significant inference inefficiency [28, 42, 66]. Recent expert skipping methods [6, 22, 42] thus propose to skip redundant experts w.r.t. current tokens to accelerate inference. However, applying these methods to MoE MLLMs leads to a significant drop in accuracy. For example, as shown in Fig. 1, skipping 83% of the experts in previous methods [6, 22,",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.15690#page=1,heuristic_unvalidated,3569
