34d20d5e612bdf8c,https://openalex.org/W7106698664,https://openalex.org/W4402671950,AnyExperts: On-Demand Expert Allocation for Multimodal Language Models with Mixture of Expert,DeepSeekMoE: Towards Ultimate Expert Specialization in Mixture-of-Experts Language Models,1,Introduction,numeric,comparison_or_baseline_signal,"architecture has emerged as a promising paradigm for efficient scaling: by sparsely activating a subset of expert subnetworks per input, MoE enables significant parameter growth while maintaining controlled computational cost [3, 33, 36] compared to traditional dense models [8, 18].","owever, their ever-increasing parameter counts have led to substantial computational overhead. To address this challenge, the Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) architecture has emerged as a promising paradigm for efficient scaling: by sparsely activating a subset of expert subnetworks per input, MoE enables significant parameter growth while maintaining controlled computational cost [3, 33, 36] compared to traditional dense models [8, 18]. However, existing MoE approaches in multimodal settings remain limited by rigid routing strategies. Most notably, they enforce a fixed number K of activated experts per token, irrespective of the input’s modality or semantic content. This one-size-fits-all allocation fails to account for the inherent heterogeneity across modalities: visual or video inputs often contain substantial redundancy (e.g., homogeneous back",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.18314#page=1,heuristic_unvalidated,4345
