7ab42ff9519a5975,https://openalex.org/W7108959160,https://openalex.org/W4404133759,Context-Aware Mixture-of-Experts Inference on CXL-Enabled GPU-NDP Systems,MoNDE: Mixture of Near-Data Experts for Large-Scale Sparse Models,1,Introduction,numeric,unknown,"To overcome this bottleneck, recent work has explored heterogeneous systems that couple GPUs with near-data processing (NDP) devices [13, 18, 33, 38].","ibuted equally to this work. over PCIe that dominate latency and reduce GPU utilization. As reported in [40], the latency of migrating an expert from the CPU to the GPU can exceed 90% of the total execution time of a Transformer block, greatly surpassing both expert and non-expert computation. To overcome this bottleneck, recent work has explored heterogeneous systems that couple GPUs with near-data processing (NDP) devices [13, 18, 33, 38]. Among these, CXL-attached memory with near-data processing (CXL-NDP) provides large-capacity DDR-class memory and high internal bandwidth. These devices can execute expert computation near memory, converting large parameter movement into small activation movement, and they support much larger MoE models at lower cost, making them a practical and promising solution. However, efficiently deploying MoE on GPU-NDP systems re",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2512.04476#page=1,heuristic_unvalidated,3044
88433ceb57041590,https://openalex.org/W7108959160,https://openalex.org/W4404133759,Context-Aware Mixture-of-Experts Inference on CXL-Enabled GPU-NDP Systems,MoNDE: Mixture of Near-Data Experts for Large-Scale Sparse Models,2,Routing,numeric,unknown,"In practice, the parameter footprint of MoE models exceeds onpackage HBM capacity, so expert parameters are placed in an external tier and fetched on demand during inference [17, 18, 31].","d a router selects a small subset per token. Given a hidden state x ∈Rd, the router R(x) produces scores w= Softmax(Wgx), and only the top-kexperts are activated. Each expert FFN typically consists of two linear layers with an intermediate activation. In practice, the parameter footprint of MoE models exceeds onpackage HBM capacity, so expert parameters are placed in an external tier and fetched on demand during inference [17, 18, 31]. The router’s per-token, per-layer decisions yield small and rapidly E0 E1 E2 E3 E4 E5 E6 E7 Expert Id 0 4 8 12 16 20 24 28 Layer Id 100000 150000 200000 250000 300000 350000 Activation Frequency Figure 2: Activation frequency of all experts in Mixtral-8x7B. changing working sets, which makes naive weight fetching particularly costly during the decoding stage. 2.2 GPU–NDP Hybrid Systems for MoE To address the memory-bound n",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2512.04476#page=2,heuristic_unvalidated,8662
fcdad402fb95a099,https://openalex.org/W7108959160,https://openalex.org/W4404133759,Context-Aware Mixture-of-Experts Inference on CXL-Enabled GPU-NDP Systems,MoNDE: Mixture of Near-Data Experts for Large-Scale Sparse Models,2,Routing,numeric,unknown,"Building on the observation that expert activations are highly skewed, recent GPU-NDP MoE systems such as MoNDE [18] and PIMoE [33] introduce the concept of hot and cold experts.","e GPUs with near-data processing (NDP) devices. Among these, CXL-attached NDP devices provide largecapacity DDR-class memory and high internal bandwidth. They can execute computations adjacent to offloaded parameters and support much larger MoE models at lower cost, making them a practical and deployable solution. Building on the observation that expert activations are highly skewed, recent GPU-NDP MoE systems such as MoNDE [18] and PIMoE [33] introduce the concept of hot and cold experts. As shown in Figure 2, which reports the activation frequency of all experts in Mixtral-8×7B [16] on the WikiText-2 [24] task, the distribution is far from uniform: a few experts are frequently activated, whereas some remain rarely used. This skew implies heterogeneous arithmetic intensities (compute-to-memory ratios) across experts, suggesting a device-aware mappin",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2512.04476#page=2,heuristic_unvalidated,9653
86af5be592c98a3b,https://openalex.org/W7108959160,https://openalex.org/W4404133759,Context-Aware Mixture-of-Experts Inference on CXL-Enabled GPU-NDP Systems,MoNDE: Mixture of Near-Data Experts for Large-Scale Sparse Models,3,Routing,numeric,unknown,"Context-Aware Mixture-of-Experts Inference on CXL-Enabled GPU–NDP Systems tier, effectively turning parameter movement into cheaper activation movement [18].","tivated, whereas some remain rarely used. This skew implies heterogeneous arithmetic intensities (compute-to-memory ratios) across experts, suggesting a device-aware mapping: pin hot, compute-intensive experts in GPU HBM, and place cold or infrequently used experts in the NDP Context-Aware Mixture-of-Experts Inference on CXL-Enabled GPU–NDP Systems tier, effectively turning parameter movement into cheaper activation movement [18]. However, prior GPU–NDP MoE systems largely rely on ondemand swapping and context-agnostic decisions at inference time. Under limited GPU↔CXL memory bandwidth, such reactive policies still incur substantial expert-transfer overheads and can reduce GPU utilization, which limits their efficiency and fails to fully exploit the inherent hot–cold characteristics of MoE experts. 2.3 Quantization for MoE Models To prevent the",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2512.04476#page=3,heuristic_unvalidated,10345
d50f88cf7dffc664,https://openalex.org/W7108959160,https://openalex.org/W4404133759,Context-Aware Mixture-of-Experts Inference on CXL-Enabled GPU-NDP Systems,MoNDE: Mixture of Near-Data Experts for Large-Scale Sparse Models,5,Model,numeric,use_signal,"To enable a fair and intuitive comparison, we adopt the same GPU–NDP system configuration used in MoNDE [18] and build our NDP system simulator on Ramulator [19] following the same methodology.","zero-shot evaluation. All accuracy results are obtained using the EleutherAI LM Evaluation Harness [10]. Table 1: Configs of evaluated MoE models Model Hidden Layers Experts Top-k Experts Params. Params. Mixtral-8×7B [16] (4096, 14336) 32 8 2 45.1B 46.7B Mixtral-8×22B [32] (6144, 16384) 56 8 2 135.5B 140.6B System Settings. To enable a fair and intuitive comparison, we adopt the same GPU–NDP system configuration used in MoNDE [18] and build our NDP system simulator on Ramulator [19] following the same methodology. The detailed configuration is summarized in Table 2. Our method migrates only a small number of highimportance experts to the GPU, while the remaining low-bitwidth experts are executed on the NDP devices. For the GPU-only baseline, all experts are loaded to the GPU on demand via PCIe. We evaluate multiple input–output length configuration",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2512.04476#page=5,heuristic_unvalidated,23889
