787ec3b7861d85cd,https://openalex.org/W7115026304,https://openalex.org/W4408858386,GateBreaker: Gate-Guided Attacks on Mixture-of-Expert LLMs,A Survey on Mixture of Experts in Large Language Models,3,Introduction,numeric,unknown,"The gating network (different than the gate-projection layer in an expert), typically a linear layer, computes a routing score for each expert based on the input token embedding x, producing a score vector that is normalized via softmax [30].","model into a higher-dimensional space (via Wup and Wgate ∈Rdff×dmodel), then applies a multiplicative interaction before projecting back to the original dimension through Wdown ∈Rdmodel×dff. The gating network (different than the gate-projection layer in an expert), typically a linear layer, computes a routing score for each expert based on the input token embedding x, producing a score vector that is normalized via softmax [30]. The top-k experts with the highest scores are selected to process the token, and their outputs may be combined using the corresponding softmax weights. This routing mechanism allows different experts to specialize in distinct linguistic or semantic phenomena. Compared to standard dense transformers, where all parameters are activated for every input, MoEs dramatically increase the model’s effective capacity while keeping",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2512.21008#page=3,heuristic_unvalidated,11401
c632b102f28696bb,https://openalex.org/W7115026304,https://openalex.org/W4408858386,GateBreaker: Gate-Guided Attacks on Mixture-of-Expert LLMs,A Survey on Mixture of Experts in Large Language Models,3,Introduction,numeric,comparison_or_baseline_signal,"Compared to standard dense transformers, where all parameters are activated for every input, MoEs dramatically increase the model’s effective capacity while keeping the computational cost roughly constant [30].","es are selected to process the token, and their outputs may be combined using the corresponding softmax weights. This routing mechanism allows different experts to specialize in distinct linguistic or semantic phenomena. Compared to standard dense transformers, where all parameters are activated for every input, MoEs dramatically increase the model’s effective capacity while keeping the computational cost roughly constant [30]. 2.2 MoE Architectures Several MoE architectures have been proposed in recent years [30]. Figure 1 demonstrates the three most representative variants: sparse, mixture, and grouped mixture MoE. F!""#$!% + ... G!(x) ... Prompt (x) Gate G""(x) G#(x) G$(x) G%(x) × × × × × TopK(-,K) f&(x) f'(x) f((x) f)(x) f*(x) (a) Sparse F!""#$%&'!(#$!%& + ... ... Prompt (x) Gate G!(x) G""(x) G#(x) G$(x) × × × × TopK(-,K) Shared E(x) f)(x) f*(x) f+(x) f,",https://arxiv.org/pdf/2512.21008#page=3,heuristic_unvalidated,11876
